                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d39d7120-7ef7-3afe-844c-c810f3ee4b62",
                        "entry_id": "735d8c91-3182-3310-bae2-276de627f907",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. возничий, сидящий на одной из передних лошадей, запряженных цугом"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "197a9e08-9431-40f0-9610-959f1b020d43",
                                "sense_id": "d39d7120-7ef7-3afe-844c-c810f3ee4b62",
                                "text": "Двести тысячонок так привлекательно стали рисоваться в голове его, что он внутренно начал досадовать на самого себя, зачем в продолжение хлопотни около экипажей не разведал от форейтора или кучера, кто такие были проезжающие."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "99220eac-19ed-4dcf-8ac4-5b425309176b",
                                "sense_id": "d39d7120-7ef7-3afe-844c-c810f3ee4b62",
                                "text": "Только раз в неделю, в воскресенье, слуги сводили старуху по беломраморной лестнице и усаживали в запряженную шестеркой старых рысаков карету, которой правил старик кучер, а на запятках стояли два ветхих лакея в шитых ливреях, и на левой лошади передней пары мотался верхом форейтор, из конюшенных «мальчиков», тоже лет шестидесяти."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f2635b0f-735f-45de-9bfb-e893c6e0a2ea",
                        "source_entry_id": "735d8c91-3182-3310-bae2-276de627f907",
                        "source_sense_id": "d39d7120-7ef7-3afe-844c-c810f3ee4b62",
                        "target_lang_word": "postilion",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "postilion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8626616e-0051-3da1-96ac-f9dc3363eecd",
                                        "entry_id": "52465d67-d47c-3657-85ea-eb8c08800028",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rider mounted on the near (left) leading horse who guides the team pulling a carriage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dec64cbc-b87e-4fa2-929d-eeea36e17afa",
                                                "sense_id": "8626616e-0051-3da1-96ac-f9dc3363eecd",
                                                "text": "C’est un garcon de bonne fortune, said the landlord, pointing through the window to half a dozen wenches who had got round about La Fleur, and were most kindly taking their leave of him, as the postilion was leading out the horses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92e61ce1-4e98-4d48-81e7-435b1d6347e7",
                                                "sense_id": "8626616e-0051-3da1-96ac-f9dc3363eecd",
                                                "text": "The postilion seized one of his fat horses by the tail, and swung himself up to his seat again."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b02ae3db-e32c-4b7d-b67c-a25a43d8a9e2",
                                                "sense_id": "8626616e-0051-3da1-96ac-f9dc3363eecd",
                                                "text": "And now the carriage had fairly left the village; yet the postilions slackened their speed, and drew up gradually before a line of almshouses, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25190953-20cf-461d-b354-ed5cddfda92d",
                                                "sense_id": "8626616e-0051-3da1-96ac-f9dc3363eecd",
                                                "text": "The rain drove into the bride and bridegroom's faces as they passed to the chariot. The postilions' favours draggled on their dripping jackets."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4102b8c-6f06-4ca7-a419-0c69cd90180a",
                                                "sense_id": "8626616e-0051-3da1-96ac-f9dc3363eecd",
                                                "text": "To play the postilion is not an easy thing. It is a trade by itself—half a gunner's and half a groom's. It has to do with horses—that is bad enough ; but also it involves some knowledge of the road."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a26bc3e-ea5b-4496-b0bd-c540ddeec259",
                                                "sense_id": "8626616e-0051-3da1-96ac-f9dc3363eecd",
                                                "text": "A very spirited affair it looked with its red body and yellow wheels, bouncing about on its high C springs [...] with its four horses going full stretch and two postilions in knee-cords and top-boots laying into the horses in a lather of dust and excitement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36dec191-2309-3bd6-a8ca-ca3a984e0dbd",
                                        "entry_id": "52465d67-d47c-3657-85ea-eb8c08800028",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A post-boy, a messenger boy, a swift letter carrier."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
